module gunbc.rung_drop.direct_call_unbound_carried_generic_compat

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, AuthoredProse, DirectCallUnboundCarriedGenericCompat }

data direct_call_unbound_carried_generic_compat: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "direct_call_unbound_carried_generic_compat" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "Direct-call argument TYPE-COMPAT when a declaration-bound formal or produced value still carries an unbound generic",

  declared: "2026-09-03",

  standing: Standing,

  declaration: AuthoredProse { legacy: DirectCallUnboundCarriedGenericCompat, authored: "**THE MODULE-WIDE `v2.*` EXEMPTION IS RETIRED, AND THIS NARROWER UNBOUND-GENERIC BOUNDARY IS DECLARED IN ITS PLACE (2026-09-03).** PREVIOUS RUNG: the compat arm was absent for every direct call in every `v2.*` module and silent when skipped. TEMPORARY RUNG: mitigatable. `v1.compiler.infer` `direct_call_arg_type_mismatch` judges every resolved direct call, but accepts when the declaration substitution basis or the produced value still carries an unbound `TypeVariable`; the sibling inhabitance judgment emits the typed, located `DeclaredTypeInhabitanceUndecided` diagnostic with reason `UndecidableGenericFormal`. Unlike the old switch, this boundary announces each occurrence and the compile-clean partition counts it as advisory rather than allowing a rendered diagnostic to belong to neither its blocking nor advisory total. REASON: synthesized constructor signatures and higher-order generic callbacks can retain a parent generic after the call substitution pass, so compatibility cannot prove nominal mismatch at that position. POPULATION, RE-DERIVABLE RATHER THAN TRANSCRIBED: run `compile_clean_diagnostic_histogram` over the required-lane closure and select diagnostic class `DeclaredTypeInhabitanceUndecided`, direct-call argument position/name, reason `UndecidableGenericFormal`; that identity set is the population and no copied count is authoritative. RESTORATION TRIGGER, NAMED AT CAPABILITY GRAIN: every generic a direct call has bound -- whether from a sibling argument, a synthesized constructor signature, or a higher-order callback formal -- is substituted into each formal before compatibility, keyed by the TypeParameter declaration and not by spelling (derived-node identity step 2, gunbc.recurring_failure_mode generic_identity_decided_by_spelling), making both the carried formal and produced value decidable without an accepting undecidable arm. SUFFICIENT FOR: `pair<U>(a: U, b: U)` called with two distinct concrete products, and `list_snoc_item(xs: List<A>, item: B)`, to refuse (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode generic_formal_unjudged_against_a_sibling_bound_argument). CORRECTED 2026-10-01: this trigger first named only synthesized constructor signatures and higher-order callback formals, which is narrower than the loss -- a plain user generic whose parameter is already bound by a sibling argument sits in the same population and would have stayed admitted after that trigger fired. A manually maintained census, a module exemption, or suppressing the advisory does not satisfy this trigger." }
}
